" Title: Shore Staff Leave Policy - Meridian Marine Ltd.\n\n1. Annual Leave\n   1.1 All shore staff are entitled to a minimum of 25 days of annual leave per calendar year, pro-rated for part-time employees. The entitlement accrues progressively throughout the year.\n\n   1.2 Unused annual leave will be carried over to the following year, but cannot exceed a total of 30 days. Any unused leave beyond this limit will be forfeited at the end of the year.\n\n2. Sick Leave\n   2.1 In case of sickness, full-time employees are entitled to 10 days of paid sick leave per calendar year. Part-time employees' entitlement is proportional to their working hours.\n\n   2.2 A medical certificate is required if the sick leave exceeds 3 consecutive days or if requested by management.\n\n3. Parental Leave\n   3.1 Eligible shore staff are entitled to a maximum of 26 weeks of parental leave for each child born or adopted, with up to 4 weeks of this period reserved as maternity leave (if applicable).\n\n   3.2 Parental leave can be taken within 52 weeks of the child's birth or adoption placement. The leave can be taken all at once or in smaller periods, subject to manager approval.\n\n4. Bereavement Leave\n   4.1 In case of death of an immediate family member, shore staff are entitled to 3 days of paid bereavement leave. Immediate family members include spouse, children, parents, siblings, and grandparents.\n\n5. Requesting Leave\n   5.1 A minimum of two weeks' notice is required when requesting annual leave, sick leave, or parental leave. In emergencies, a shorter notice may be acceptable but must be approved by management.\n\n   5.2 Bereavement leave can be taken immediately upon notification of the death and does not require prior notice.\n\n6. Leave Approval\n   6.1 All leave requests should be submitted through the HR department's online portal. The request will then be reviewed by the employee's direct supervisor, who may consult with relevant colleagues or management as needed.\n\n   6.2 Employees will receive written confirmation of their leave approval or denial within 5 business days of submitting their request. If additional information is required to make a decision, the employee will be notified promptly.\n\n7. Returning from Leave\n   7.1 Upon returning from any form of leave, employees are expected to submit a brief report outlining their absence and any necessary arrangements for catching up on missed work. This report should be submitted through the HR department's online portal.\n\n   7.2 Employees returning from parental leave will have a period of 4 weeks to adjust to their return, during which they may work reduced hours or flex hours as agreed with their supervisor.\n\n8. Exceptions and Special Cases\n   8.1 In some cases, exceptions to this policy may be granted at the discretion of management due to exceptional circumstances or for operational reasons. These exceptions will be documented and communicated to the affected employee in writing.\n\n8.2 Shore staff who believe they have grounds for an exception should submit a written request outlining their case through the HR department."